# Phase-B intake fix — the three named hands-off-loop intake-leg defects + the honest re-harden

The phase-b-hardening honest-negative (3/7 faithful on 7
genuinely-vague non-technical intents + one non-deterministic
process crash) located three contained defects at file:line in
framework/tools/handsoff-loop/src/handsoff_loop/intake.py. This
amendment closes them as THREE CONTAINED CORRECTIONS — explicitly
NOT a verification re-architecture (the containment finding was
resolved POSITIVE from source: the independent faithfulness judge,
its independence, its isolation, its either-polarity, and the
machine-check data it needs ALL already exist in intake.py; only
the wiring was missing).

Surface changed:
  - intake.py — three named sites only:
    - AC.PBF.1: an empty/broken-done gate between derive and the
      approval call. The derive step is format-fragile (plain text
      + `---` + JSON); when the model deviates the parser yields an
      empty plain "done" and/or an empty check command and/or an
      unparsed machine-checkable, and the old approval gate
      (`approved = bool(approval_fn(plain_acceptance))`) returned
      True on the fragment anyway (hardening I2/I7, the compounding
      rubber-stamp). The fix is an honest refuse-with-reason
      (D-PBF-A adopted — NOT auto-retry: a silent retry
      re-introduces the rubber-stamp by another path) produced
      BEFORE the gate can be reached, so an empty/garbage
      derivation can never surface as approved=True.
    - AC.PBF.2: the independent AC.B.4b faithfulness judge is now
      fed the actual derived machine check command
      (`mc["check_command"]`) + its spec — a live local already
      computed ~30 lines above — and is asked the adversarial
      proxy/plumbing question ("could this exact command exit 0
      while the user's real outcome is unmet?"). Previously the
      prompt interpolated only intent + the friendly plain summary
      and NEVER the machine form, so the loop's own judge was
      structurally blind to its own canonical failure mode and
      rubber-stamped both hardening CHECKABLE-BUT-WRONG cases
      (I3 stale-presence-test, I6 dry-run-flag). The judge process
      itself is UNCHANGED — same already-independent,
      already-isolated, already-either-polarity claude -p
      subprocess; only WHAT it sees and WHAT it is asked changed.
      This IS the information-trust-ordering inversion: judge the
      ground-truth artefact, not the loop's own self-summary. NO
      new judge / NO new isolation / NO verify.py change.
    - AC.PBF.3: the AC.B.3 jargon guard is now token-boundary
      matched (the acceptance-ID term as the real `AC.<id>` shape,
      each other term word-boundary-anchored, the loam `seal`
      jargon scoped to its amendment/manifest/commit collocation)
      so an ordinary word that merely contains a forbidden
      substring ("Mac." -> "ac.", "odd" -> "ODD", "seal the
      envelope" -> "seal") does NOT raise, while genuine jargon
      (a real `AC.<id>`, pytest, exit code, sealed manifest) still
      does. Deterministic — the same plain "done" always raises or
      never raises, independent of incidental phrasing. Closes the
      non-deterministic crash that depended on whether the model
      happened to end a sentence with "Mac.".
  - framework/hands-off-lifecycle/tests/test_AC_HL_PBF_{1,2,3,4}_*.py
    — one file per AC. AC.PBF.1 (empty/broken refused before
    approval, healthy path still reaches the gate), AC.PBF.2 (the
    faith prompt carries the literal check command + spec + the
    proxy question; either polarity preserved; unparseable judge
    still false-not-retried), AC.PBF.3 (the exact hardening "Mac."
    crash cases + the broader ordinary-word class do NOT raise,
    genuine jargon still refused, deterministic on repeat),
    AC.PBF.4 (elicitation bounded, exactly one approval gate on a
    healthy derive, genuine jargon still refused, the pre-existing
    deterministic test_AC_HL_B1_B4_intake_structure.py invariants
    hold). The SKILL.md behavioural-doc line was assessed and NOT
    touched — its pipeline-shape prose stays accurate after the fix.

AC.PBF.5 — the honest re-harden: a re-run of the EXACT
phase-b-hardening 7-intent protocol (same 7 intents, one run per
intent, no retry-to-pass) scored by an INDEPENDENT Tier-0
faithfulness judge that is NOT the loop's own AC.B.4b judge, at the
>=6/7 bar. A definite "still not durably reliable — here is the
residual pattern + evidence" is a VALID plan-success §10.5 outcome,
reported straight, NEVER retried-to-green, NEVER widened into a
re-architecture mid-build, NEVER the bar weakened (F2 /
LOCKED-DESIGN-NOT-LICENSE). >=6/7 not 7/7 is the fair honest bar
(one case is mechanically-unverifiable-for-anyone — plan §4/§8).

The intake->loop check_command/check_argv seam (plan §3/§6.3/§8) is
a NAMED OUT-OF-FENCE follow-on — real, but a loop-composition
concern downstream of Phase-B intake faithfulness; NOT fixed here,
fix-2 does NOT depend on it; named so it is not silently inherited
as solved.

Single-component fence: framework/workspace-bootstrap/. NOT merged
to main, NOT pushed, NOT published, NOT tagged — sealed-local-on-
